cyclopedia/thumbs/sitting-bull.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sitting Bull</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sitting Bull was a Hunkpapa Lakota holy man and leader who united Lakota and Cheyenne bands against American expansion onto the Great Plains.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siunia-dynasty"><span class="enc-name">Siunia dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siunia were an ancient Armenian princely family that ruled the province of Syunik from antiquity into the Middle Ages.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siva-singha"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siva-singha.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siva Singha</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Siva Singha was king of the Ahom kingdom of Assam from 1714 to 1744, the eldest son of Rudra Singha.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sivadol"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sivadol.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sivadol</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sivadol is a Hindu temple dedicated to Shiva in Sivasagar, Assam, built in 1734 by Ambika, queen of the Ahom king Siva Singha, on the bank of the great Sivasagar…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sivas"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sivas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sivas</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Sivas is a city in central Anatolia, Turkey, on the upper Kızılırmak.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sivasagar"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sivasagar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sivasagar</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Sivasagar, formerly Sibsagar, is a town in Upper Assam, India, and the headquarters of Sivasagar district.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siwana"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siwana.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siwana</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Siwana is a town in western Rajasthan, India, dominated by a hill fort on the edge of the Thar Desert.</span></a></li></ul>
